    <innerclass refid="classEntityControllerBase" prot="public">EntityControllerBase</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract contract for the request-facing CRUDS handlers exposed for every entity type. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares <computeroutput><ref refid="classEntityControllerBase" kindref="compound">EntityControllerBase</ref></computeroutput>, a pure interface: it lists the ten operations (Create/Read/ Update/Delete/Search and their Async twins) that every ordinary entity handler must provide. It contains no implementation at all - each method ends in <computeroutput>= 0</computeroutput>, meaning &quot;derived classes must fill this in&quot;.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It is the contract between the HTTP routing layer and the concrete <ref refid="classEntityController" kindref="compound">EntityController&lt;T&gt;</ref>. Drogon handlers program against this base type, so they can treat a <ref refid="classUser" kindref="compound">User</ref>, a <ref refid="classPatient" kindref="compound">Patient</ref> or a Report uniformly. Without this interface the router would have to know every entity type, and there would be no single place guaranteeing that all entities expose the same CRUDS operations. The real work is done by <ref refid="classEntityController" kindref="compound">EntityController</ref> (see <ref refid="entitycontroller_8hpp" kindref="compound">entitycontroller.hpp</ref>), which implements everything declared here.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Virtual functions / polymorphism: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/virtual">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/virtual</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Abstract classes and pure virtual functions (<computeroutput>= 0</computeroutput>): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/abstract_class">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/abstract_class</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Callback / std::function: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Coroutines (co_await / drogon::Task): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::optional and std::string_view: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
